<title>USA: Money Store sells $300 mln in 2-part deal.</title>
<headline>Money Store sells $300 mln in 2-part deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue from The Money Store Inc was priced on Thursday, according to lead manager Bear Stearns &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>BORROWER THE MONEY STORE INC</p>
<p>AMT $175 MLN	 COUPON 8.05 PCT   MATURITY 4/15/2002</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE  100.00 FIRST PAY DATE 10/15/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BA1   YIELD 8.05 PCT    PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB	 SPREAD +128 BP    CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>AMT $125 MLN	 COUPON 8.375 PCT  MATURITY 4/15/2004</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE 10/15/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BA1   YIELD 8.375 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB	 SPREAD +150 BP    CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1678))</p>
